  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of inter halogens from the following having square pyramidal structure is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ClF</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Square pyramidal structures are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>These molecules are&nbsp;made up of 6 equally spaced <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybrid orbitals arranged at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math> angles. The shape of the orbitals is octahedral. One orbital contains a lone pair of electrons, so the remaining five atoms connected to the central atom gives the molecule a square pyramidal shape. Among the given options the structure with five bond pairs and one lone pair is these three structures only.</p></blockquote>"
  }
